  "term": "verbal thought",
  "definition": "Verbal thought is thinking in which words and meaning form one continuous mental process rather than separate events. At any moment, one word may stand out most clearly, but it is experienced as carrying the wider idea, with the rest of the thought still present in the background to different degrees.",
